    "knowledge_point": "Computing Second Order Derivatives",
    "problem": "Find ${f}^{″}(x)$ for $f(x)=4\\sqrt{x}+5{x}^{2}+x.$",
    "worked_solution": "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(4\\sqrt{x}+5{x}^{2}+x)}^{′} \\\\  & ={(4{x}^{1/2}+5{x}^{2}+x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4{x}^{-1/2}+2\\cdot 5x+1 \\\\  & =2{x}^{-1/2}+10x+1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x) & ={(2{x}^{-1/2}+10x+1)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2{x}^{-3/2}+10+0 \\\\  & =-{x}^{-3/2}+10 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}+10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
